Package: dMod2
Type: Package
Title: Parameter Estimation in Dynamical Models
Version: 0.15.7
Date: 2026-11-14
Authors@R: c(
    person("Simon", "Beyer", email = "simon.beyer@fdm.uni-freiburg.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Daniel", "Kaschek", email = "daniel.kaschek@gmail.com", role = "aut",
           comment = "Created dMod 1.0; original design, philosophy"))
Description: Ordinary differential equation (ODE) models of reaction
    networks are built symbolically, compiled to 'C' or 'C++' code with
    first- and second-order sensitivities and fitted to data, following
    Kaschek et al. (2019) <doi:10.18637/jss.v088.i10>. The package succeeds
    'dMod' with a new interface and the 'cppDE' solver backend. Prediction,
    observation and objective functions compose by the chain rule and return
    derivatives with their values. Fits use trust-region optimization with
    multi-start search and profile likelihood, also for mixed-effects models.
    Models and data are exchanged in the 'PEtab' format for parameter
    estimation problems and in the Systems Biology Markup Language ('SBML').
